QA4 pre-existing 1. A wrapper is written after it was built, through a pointer
to it: a builder method stores the cause after the literal, which stores none.
The wrapper is returned: its Wrap holds, besides what the literal stored, what
the later writers of the field store, flagged as location values. (Run time
has the later value only; errtrace does not order the stores.)
